      "transcriber_notes": [
        "No column headed 'Symbol' or 'Remarks' is printed: each part prints the symbols unheaded, with the heading 'Corresponding sound in Roman Letters'; 'Remarks' holds the bracketed side-note printed beside ㄐ/ㄑ.",
        "Each part is printed in two side-by-side columns; transcribed as one list, left column top to bottom, then right column.",
        "Symbols are given with Unicode Bopomofo characters matching the printed shapes (e.g. ㄪ printed like 万, ㄎ like 丂, ㄫ like 兀); ㄧ is printed as a horizontal stroke (一). Derived finals are printed as two symbols stacked vertically and are written here as the two symbols in top-to-bottom order.",
        "Consonants ㄐ (dji) and ㄑ (chi): one brace joins both rows to the side-note, repeated in the Remarks cell of both rows.",
        "ㄖ: printed 'j (in French)' and on the next line 'ĵ (in Esperanto)' (circumflex over j) with no 'or' between them; ㄏ: 'ĥ' printed with circumflex over h.",
        "Finals: ㄜ printed 'ẽ' (tilde over e); ㄞ 'ă + i' — the i after '+' shows no dot (damaged/dotless type), written 'i'. ㄢ 'ăn' and ㄣ 'ĕn' carry breves. Angle brackets ⟨ ⟩ as printed.",
        "Derived finals: 'ia' — dot of the i faint; ㄨㄛ printed 'uo' with the o appearing open like 'ɔ' (damaged type), written 'uo'; ㄩㄥ printed 'iung' as printed (not 'üng').",
        "Chinese in part headings: 聲母, 韵母 and 結合韵母 as printed (韵 form with 勻 component).",
        "62 data rows counted on the pages; 62 transcribed. Row counts: 24 consonants counted on p. 549, 24 transcribed; 16 finals counted on p. 550, 16 transcribed (heading says 15, 'actually 16'); 22 derived finals counted on p. 550, 22 transcribed."
      ],
